{"authored" [{"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠BAC$ given the points $A(2,1,-1)$, $B(3,-2,2)$, and $C(-1,-2,1).$ Round your answer to the nearest degree." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3c4ae64d9a3b82d1d472628be6b7d38a56c75262d035fbf1513196b1932ceac9" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{112}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{18}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{48}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{54}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{88}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{54}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c138e79e69852f73c5d8d62bcc01cfaeaeb160d75072882928b7f2f20f0df35" "basis" 650 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the points $A(2t,-1,5)$, $B(-3,t,1)$ and $C(2t+1,2,-t).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=5.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2t,\\,-1,\\,5⟩,\\,b=⟨-3,\\,t,\\,1⟩,\\,c=⟨2t+1,\\,2,\\,-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,t,\\,1⟩-⟨2t,\\,-1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-2t,\\,t+1,\\,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2t+1,\\,2,\\,-t⟩-⟨2t,\\,-1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,3,\\,-t-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=5$, we can solve for $t$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =5 \\\\ (-3-2t)\\cdot 1+(t+1)\\cdot 3+-4\\cdot (-t-5) & =5 \\\\ -3-2t+3t+3+4t+20 & =5 \\\\ 5t+20 & =5 \\\\ 5t & =-15 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨-3-2(-3),(-3)+1,-4⟩, \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,-4⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =1,\\,3,\\,-(-3)-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{406}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{406}})≈{75.63}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60cd1315cf2b6b75f4b50b0389fd8558a2160d0ff8f42305f4c35d7522a171fd" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e881b26563a6ae4d8b2da04154e4434506f1e9823304e0edb7c0e824" "basis" 843 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{71.36}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978202/state.json" "file_sha256" "ae685cf4e8