estion-capture/13978202/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(3,3,-5)$, $Q(4,2,-3)$, and $R(7,5,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨3,3,-5⟩,\\,q=⟨4,2,-3⟩,\\,r=⟨7,5,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-3⟩-⟨3,3,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨7,5,-3⟩-⟨3,3,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78041014569dbb2eb920179920355104fa61b75704067f0685f412217be6959c" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{180}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{30}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{45}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{60}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{90}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{60}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a640d249d816721c007b22d83d6a4adf87213239913229a7030d51d082d2aea" "basis" 1318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038738/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the points $A(2t,4,3),$ $B(5t-1,4,3)$ and $C(2t+4,t+5,3).$ Find $∠BAC$ given that $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,b=⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩,\\,c=⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨5t-1,\\,4,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3t-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨2t+4,\\,t+5,\\,3⟩-⟨2t,\\,4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,t+1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}=8,$ we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =8 \\\\ (3t-1)\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (t+1)+0\\cdot 0 & =8 \\\\ 4(3t-1)+0+0 & =8 \\\\ 12t-4 & =8 \\\\ 12t & =12 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0,0⟩, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{80}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}})≈{26.57}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6ec99b73bd0e45287c6205dca701f4d8435e073bd05cb9cfc6c557ae7078ee9b" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5561ca8a59b2eaedeef88d63f3cd36dea9b3abbe7b944cd99b6db533f584f7" "basis" 1409 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040103/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77167" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value"